.TH printenv 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
printenv \- print the environment, or one variable of it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B printenv
[\fIname\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no argument,
.B printenv
prints the whole environment as
.IB name = value
lines.  With a
.IR name ,
it prints just that variable value.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 if
.I name
was given and is not set; 0 otherwise.
.SH NOTES
Only the first argument is looked at; the rest are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# printenv
# printenv PATH
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR env (1),
.BR sh (1)
